Subject: [PATCH 4/6] F635-6: V16_PROJECTILE_DAMAGE_BUG gone (data 16.635.3): a
 pellet dooms its target with its own damage

Data 16.635.3 drops the global V16_PROJECTILE_DAMAGE_BUG (with V16_AEO_OWNERSHIP_BUG and
V16_RUNE_GIANT_VISUAL_BUG, which crforge does not read). A global the tables no longer publish is
read as clear (globalFlagOrClear), the bug's fix running. Clear, a travelling hit just queued
dooms its target for the rest of its volley when its own damage reaches the target's hit points,
as this global's own reading in crforge has it; the queued total is not read. Inferred from the
tables, no recorded match tells set from clear (b); the alternative, the set rule kept with the
global gone, is not excluded.
BattleTravellingHitDrainTest: its three set-rule tests set the global whatever the tables; a new
test holds the rule with the global gone (every pellet of the killing volley stops at the ram).
Core tests: 16.402.22 2148/0; 16.635.3 (guard bypassed for the run) 11 -> 3 failures.
